[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Trading Standards]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.53]Lesson 8 | 第8课
[00:01.60]Trading standards | 贸易标准
[00:07.22]What makes trading between rich countries difficult? | 是什么使富国之间的贸易困难重重？
[00:13.09]Chickens slaughtered in the United States, claim officials in Brussels, are not fit to grace European tables. | 布鲁塞尔的官员们声称，在美国屠宰的鸡不配上欧洲人的餐桌。
[00:22.00]No, say the Americans: our fowl are fine, we simply clean them in a different way. | 不，美国人说：我们的家禽好得很，我们只是用了另一种清洗方式而已。
[00:28.94]These days, it is differences in national regulations, far more than tariffs, that put sand in the wheels of trade between rich countries. | 如今，正是各国法规的差异，而远非关税，给富国之间的贸易设置了重重障碍。
[00:39.33]It is not just farmers who are complaining. | 抱怨的不只是农民。
[00:42.33]An electric razor that meets the European Union's safety standards must be approved by American testers before it can be sold in the United States, and an American-made dialysis machine needs the EU's okay before it hits the market in Europe. | 一把符合欧盟安全标准的电动剃须刀必须先得到美国检测人员的认可，然后才能在美国销售；而一台美国制造的透析机在打入欧洲市场前，也需要欧盟的批准。
[01:01.16]As it happens, a razor that is safe in Europe is unlikely to electrocute Americans. | 事实上，在欧洲使用安全的剃须刀不太可能会电死美国人。
[01:07.60]So, ask businesses on both sides of the Atlantic, why have two lots of tests where one would do? | 因此，大西洋两岸的商界要问：既然一套测试就够了，为什么要搞两套呢？
[01:15.57]Politicians agree, in principle, so America and the EU have been trying to reach a deal which would eliminate the need to double-test many products. | 政治家们在原则上表示同意，所以美国和欧盟一直在努力达成一项协议，以取消对许多产品进行双重检测的必要。
[01:25.21]They hope to finish in time for a trade summit between America and the EU on May 28th. | 他们希望能在5月28日美欧贸易峰会召开之前及时完成。
[01:32.01]Although negotiators are optimistic, the details are complex enough that they may be hard-pressed to get a deal at all. | 尽管谈判者持乐观态度，但细节相当复杂，他们可能很难达成任何协议。
[01:40.07]Why? One difficulty is to construct the agreements. | 为什么？一个难题是协议本身的构建。
[01:44.69]The Americans would happily reach one accord on standards for medical devices and then hammer out different pacts covering, say, electronic goods and drug manufacturing. | 美国人很乐意先就医疗器械的标准达成一个协议，然后再敲定分别涉及譬如电子产品和药品生产的不同协议。
[01:56.39]The EU -- following fine continental traditions -- wants agreement on general principles, | 而欧盟——遵循优秀的欧洲大陆传统——则希望就总原则达成协议，
[02:02.77]which could be applied to many types of products and perhaps extended to other countries. | 这些原则既可适用于多种类型的产品，也可能推广到其他国家。
